The remark after Proposition 4.2, and the preamble of Corollary 4.3, state \(x = \bigsqcup_n i_{n\infty}(x_n)\). That identity is [`inverseLimit.eq_iSup`](1972_inverseLimit.md). `idInf_eq_iSup` is the identity Scott map as \(\bigsqcup_n i_{n\infty} \circ j_{\infty n}\), by evaluating that supremum with `inverseLimit.eq_iSup`. Theorem 4.4 invokes this identity and does not reprove it. **Theorem:** yes — the identity of the limit is formalized. **Proof:** yes — the evaluation of the supremum of the approximating projections.
